Both units are head-side CHANGELOG.md text (lines 389-615 and 616+). They are documentation only, and no source, patch hunks or diff markers were supplied, so the specific changed lines cannot be isolated.

The entries describe several security-relevant behaviors:
- graceful draining of accepted inference across restarts and updates;
- App Attest generic apple_error retry with bounded backoff, mapped to T-057 and T-053;
- early first-assertion retry while a risk receipt is pending, mapped to T-052 and A-016;
- unenroll foreground sudo inventory, mapped to T-057;
- privacy description wording, mapped to T-056 and A-001;
- unified verification labels without exposing Apple evidence, mapped to T-058;
- admin OTP JSON encoding, mapped to TB-006 and T-026;
- Responses instructions and media routing, mapped to T-049;
- output-token budget validation;
- persisted App Attest build qualification and revocation refresh, mapped to A-017 and T-054;
- staged signed artifact publication, mapped to T-054;
- SSD disk budget and cache epoch changes, mapped to T-041.

These claims are consistent with the canonical threat-model header notes, for example the 2026-09-21/22/27 App Attest notes and the T-041 SSD disk policy.

The changelog text alone does not support a concrete regression. The next pass should verify the actual source behind these claims:
- coordinator/appattest/service: retry not extending grants;
- the qualification snapshot's 30s bound;
- final-dispatch fencing;
- KVCacheSSD policy: 20 GiB reserve and TTL of at most 1800s;
- the admin OTP JSON encoder;
- drain paths preserving cancel/terminal billing.
